# 🎉 Welcome to the Otto-Friedrich-University Bamberg! 🚀

We are pleased to welcome you as a new member of our team! This onboarding issue will guide you through your first steps. Please complete each item and check it off as you go. If you have any questions, feel free to ask for support.

## 📌 Table of Contents
- [Preparation](#preparation)
- [Your First Day at Work](#your-first-day-at-work)
- [Opportunities After the First Day](#opportunities-after-the-first-day)

---

## ✅ Preparation
- [ ] Supervisor has created your email account (IAM-Portal: Antrag auf ein persönliches Nutzerkonto inkl. E-Mail-Konto)
- [ ] Review the [team handbook](#) to understand our values, goals, and collaboration principles
- [ ] Set up your University ID (BA number) for system access

---

## 🏁 Your First Day at Work
### 🔹 Administrative Setup
- [ ] Bring your **University Card** to work
- [ ] Meet with your **mentor**, who will guide you through your first day
- [ ] Receive your **personal induction plan** from your mentor

### 🏛 Introduction to the University
- [ ] Learn about the **history, mission, and values** of the University
- [ ] Get an overview of the **organizational structure and departments**
- [ ] Familiarize yourself with the **campus layout and key locations**

### 🖥 Your Workplace
- [ ] Get introduced to your **workspace and equipment**
- [ ] Understand **building, office, and facility access**
- [ ] Set up your **IT resources** (computers, email, network accounts)

### 👥 Introduction to Your Role & Team
- [ ] Meet with your **supervisor and colleagues**
- [ ] Understand your **responsibilities and expectations**
- [ ] Learn about the **team structure and collaborations**
- [ ] Join your colleagues for **lunch** 🍽

### 🏢 Settling In
Now you can say goodbye to your mentor and spend your first few hours at work:
- [ ] Log into your **workstation** with your BA number
- [ ] Read our **values and goals**
- [ ] Explore the **organizational structure** (team roles and availabilities)
- [ ] Review the **handbook** to learn how to contribute
- [ ] Set up your **GitHub account**, upload a photo/avatar, and update your availabilities in the org page
- [ ] Read our sections on **security and emergency procedures**
- [ ] (PhD Students) **Sign and submit your ethics statement**
- [ ] Register for **VC or FlexNow**, if necessary
- [ ] Register for **VC-Kurs: Aktuelle Informationen der Fachschaft WIAI**
- [ ] Request to join the [Digital Work Lab team](#)

🎉 **Take a moment to celebrate your first successful day!** 🎉

---

## 🌟 Opportunities After the First Day
- **Job Shadowing:** Arrange a day with an experienced colleague if you need further support.
- **Social Integration & University Life:**
  - Attend the **University of Bamberg Summer Festival** 🎊
  - Visit the **Schwof @LiveClub** on Mondays to socialize with new colleagues 🎶
  - **Join Feki.de e.V.**, the largest university student group for networking and information exchange

---

🔹 If you have any questions, don't hesitate to ask! Welcome aboard, and we look forward to working with you! 🚀
